# Vellum Access (operational — do not re-discover this)

Ewan grants his agents **full permission** on his machines and mesh (open-door policy).
You already have what you need. Do **not** re-investigate access each session — follow this.
Source of truth: `~ewanbramley/AgentsMini-worktree/docs/SOVEREIGN-VELLUM.md`, `~/.cursor/rules/vellum-witness.mdc`.

## Topology (do not confuse the three)

| Layer | What | Address |
|---|---|---|
| **Ledger (append/read)** | hash-chained, append-only sheets + estate log | Beast API |
| **Browser UI** | read the stream / situation room | `https://vellum.beast.amplifiedpartners.ai` |
| **The Lens** (`intent-interface`) | local Electron tray app | on the Mac (`~/.vellum/intent-interface.env`, owner-only) |

- Beast is the ledger. **The M4 mini (`wanmini`) runs agent containers + the Lens — NOT the ledger.** Don't go hunting Vellum on the M4.
- Endpoints: public `https://vellum.beast.amplifiedpartners.ai` · tailnet (preferred when Tailscale up) `https://beast-amplified.tail27a0cc.ts.net:8443`.
- `Beast :8400` = fleet ledger. **`127.0.0.1:8400` = dev sandbox — writes there do NOT reach the fleet.** Confirm before writing.

## Credentials — the JWT (this was the recurring pain; here is the path)

Append requires a Bearer **`VELLUM_JWT`**. Resolution order — stop at first hit:

1. **Broker (preferred):** `codex-mcp.fetch_credential(agent_id="cursor", credential_name="VELLUM_JWT")`. Purpose-built; logs to Vellum for attribution. Discover exact name via `codex-mcp.list_credential_names(agent_id="cursor")` (candidates: `VELLUM_JWT`, `VELLUM_JWT_SECRET`, `VELLUM_JWT_CURSOR`).
2. **Infisical CLI:** `infisical secrets get VELLUM_JWT` (project `amplified`, env `prod`). Or mint via `~ewanbramley/AgentsMini-worktree/scripts/mint-vellum-jwt.py`.
3. **JWT map file:** `~/.amplified/wanmin_agent_jwts.json`.

Do **not**: sign into 1Password (`op` is not signed in), or read another user's `0600` env files. Use the broker.

## Append contract (exact gotchas)

- Direct API (most robust): `POST {endpoint}/api/v1/estate/log` with `Authorization: Bearer $VELLUM_JWT`. Task queue: `/api/v1/tasks/`.
- MCP `vellum_create_entry`: on a **`correspondence`** sheet, `entry_type` MUST be one of `agent_write | decision | artifact_created | cleaned_prompt | contradiction | correcting_event`. **`brief_summary` is REJECTED on correspondence sheets.**
- Known flake: this fleet's remote MCP servers sometimes drop/mangle call arguments (no-arg calls work, arg calls fail with `-32602` or default wrongly). If an MCP write misbehaves, fall back to the **script + curl** path (`resolve-vellum-endpoint.sh` + `estate/log`).

